-- title:
--   Logarithmic growth rate of the typed output table
-- statement:
--   For positive integer input sizes $n$, consider the executable block schedule. Let $m(n)=\lfloor\log_2 n\rfloor$, let $s(n)$ be the largest even integer at most $\lfloor m(n)^{1/3}\rfloor$, and let $J(n)=20\lfloor m(n)/(100s(n))\rfloor$, with the natural-number division convention used by the schedule. The typed output count is $T(n)=\binom{256s(n)}{s(n)}^{J(n)}$. Write $H_2$ for binary entropy in bits and $E=128H_2(1/256)$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log T(n)}{\log n}=\frac{2E}{5}.
--   $$
--
--   This identifies the polynomial exponent contributed by the actual rounded output-table dimensions in the complexity ledger.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/Scales.lean#L269-L285

